1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Hello, we're delegates representing District 3.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Here is an example of trial flow.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,000
All rise.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
The 108th District Court is now in session.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Honorable Judge Kennedy presiding.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Thank you. You may be seated.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Court is now in session.

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
We call Case Number 1, 2, 3, 4, 5.

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The State of Texas versus Miley Cyrus is now in session.

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Is the prosecution ready?

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Yes, Your Honor.

12
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Is the defense ready?

13
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,000
We are, Your Honor.

14
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Okay. We will now hear opening statements from the prosecution.

15
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Thank you, Your Honor.

16
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Your Honor, my name is Kevin Metz and this is my co-counsel, Krista Quinones.

17
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:56,000
We represent the State of Texas today, and today you will hear how Miley Cyrus, the defendant in this case, broke into the store of young Emma Watson.

18
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
We will prove that she was trespassing, and Your Honor, this is why we ask for a verdict of guilty. Thank you.

19
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Thank you, counsel.

20
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Would the defense like to give their opening now, or would they like to defer until the prosecution rests their case?

21
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,000
We would like to give our opening statement now, Your Honor.

22
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,000
You may.

23
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Your Honor, ladies and gentlemen of the court, my name is Jessie Kelly and this is my co-counsel, Kevin Hawley.

24
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Today we are representing the defendant, Miley Cyrus, in the case of the State of Texas versus Miley Cyrus.

25
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,000
She is being accused of breaking into Emma Watson's store, even though she was clearly at a party that night.

26
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:35,000
She never broke into Emma Watson's store. Your Honor, we ask for a verdict of not guilty.

27
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Thank you, counsel. Will the prosecution please call their first witness?

28
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Yes, Your Honor. The prosecution would like to call Emma Watson to the stand.

29
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Emma Watson, please take the stand.

30
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Ms. Watson, before you sit, can you please stand and raise your right hand?

31
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Do you swear to tell the whole truth and nothing but the truth to help you God?

32
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,000
I do.

33
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,000
You may be seated.

34
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Ms. Watson, please introduce yourself.

35
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,000
My name is Emma Watson and I am an actress in the movie.

36
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Could you tell us a little bit about your profession as a store owner?

37
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:16,000
I've been in the store since 2000 and I am currently the manager.

38
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:21,000
On January 1st, what did you see when you arrived at your store?

39
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:29,000
I saw a lady breaking into my store with a tattoo on her right arm and I later figured out that it was the same tattoo as Miley Cyrus'.

40
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Who do you think that woman was?

41
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Miley Cyrus.

42
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Pass the witness.

43
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Thank you, counsel. Will the defense like to cross?

44
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Yes, Your Honor.

45
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,000
You may begin.

46
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Ms. Watson, were there any surveillance cameras in your store?

47
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,000
No, there were not.

48
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Then how did you know it was Miley Cyrus'?

49
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Well, she had the same tattoo as Miley Cyrus' and she had brightly colored short hair like Miley Cyrus'.

50
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Pass the witness, Your Honor.

51
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Thank you, counsel. Would the prosecution like to redirect?

52
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Yes, Your Honor.

53
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
You may begin.

54
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Ms. Watson, how many people do you know have the same tattoos as Miley Cyrus'?

55
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Only Miley Cyrus'.

56
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Pass the witness.

57
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Thank you, counsel. Would the defense like to recross?

58
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,000
No, Your Honor.

59
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Emma Watson, you may sit down. Does the prosecution have any more witnesses to call?

60
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
No, Your Honor. The prosecution rests.

61
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Thank you, counsel. Will the defense please call their first witness?

62
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,000
The defense calls Miley Cyrus to the stand.

63
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Miley Cyrus, please take the stand.

64
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Ms. Cyrus, can you please stand real fast? Please raise your right hand.

65
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Do you swear to tell the truth, the whole truth, and nothing but the truth to help you God?

66
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:46,000
I do.

67
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Thank you. You may be seated.

68
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,000
May I make it my line of questioning, Your Honor?

69
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,000
You may.

70
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Would you please state your name for the benefit of the court?

71
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
My name is Miley Cyrus.

72
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:02,000
And where were you on the accused night of your break-in at Emma Watson's store?

73
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,000
I was at a party.

74
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,000
And what do you remember from this party?

75
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Nothing.

76
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,000
You may pass the witness, Your Honor.

77
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Thank you, counsel. Is the prosecution ready to cross?

78
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Yes, Your Honor.

79
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,000
You may begin.

80
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Ms. Cyrus, can you just repeat what you remember from the night of your party you were at?

81
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,000
I don't remember anything.

82
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,000
Is that because you broke into a store?

83
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,000
I don't know.

84
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Do you know if you broke into a store?

85
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Not really.

86
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Pass the witness.

87
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Thank you, counsel. Would the defense like to redirect?

88
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,000
Yes, Your Honor.

89
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
You may begin.

90
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:43,000
Just to restate, you don't remember anything from the night of that party, do you?

91
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,000
No.

92
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:49,000
So you could have been...could you have been at the party the entire time?

93
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Oh, absolutely.

94
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Pass the witness, Your Honor.

95
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:55,000
Thank you, counsel. Would the prosecution like to cross?

96
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Briefly, Your Honor.

97
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,000
You may begin.

98
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Ms. Cyrus, why was it that you could not remember what was going on that night?

99
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Well, my friend said I had a few beers and I guess I passed out a little, but I could surely understand where I was at.

100
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Well, I don't know, actually.

101
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Pass the witness.

102
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Thank you, counsel.

103
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Ms. Cyrus, you may step down.

104
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Does the defense have any more witnesses to call?

105
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
No, Your Honor. The defense rests their case.

106
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Thank you. We will now hear closing statements on behalf of the state.

107
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Your Honor, today we have the burden of proof.

108
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
You saw Miley Cyrus as guilty of trespassing.

109
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Our witness Emma Stone told us she saw Cyrus breaking the law.

110
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,000
We ask for your verdict of guilty.

111
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Thank you, counsel.

112
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,000
Would you like to save any remaining time for rebuttal?

113
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,000
No, thank you, Your Honor.

114
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:53,000
Defense, you may give your closing statement.

115
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,000
Thank you, Your Honor. May I begin?

116
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,000
You may.

117
00:05:55,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Your Honor, today the prosecution has the burden of proof, and they have failed to prove it.

118
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:10,000
Your Honor, they have not shown beyond original doubt that Miley Cyrus did indeed break into Emma Watson's store and be guilty of breaking and injuring.

119
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:16,000
As the prosecution has not proven this fact, we urge a not guilty verdict, Your Honor.

120
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Thank you.

121
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Thank you. All rise.

122
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:25,000
The court will now be in recess while I deliberate.

123
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:28,000
All rise.

124
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:35,000
The 108th District Court is now in session, Honorable Judge Kennedy presiding.

125
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,000
Thank you. You may be seated.

126
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:46,000
In case number 1.2345, the state of Texas versus Miley Cyrus, I find Ms. Cyrus not guilty of trespassing.

127
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:54,000
In case number 1.2345, the state of Texas versus Miley Cyrus, I find Ms. Cyrus not guilty of trespassing.

